window.PYQ_OCR['ssc-chsl'].push({t:'ssc chsl 2022 tier2 26 jun',q:[{"n": 1, "q": "Ans 1. 1 2. −1 3. 0 4. 2 Question ID : 264330144227 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 3", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 2, "q": "The HCF of two numbers is one-twentieth of their LCM. If one of the numbers is 96 and the difference of the LCM and the HCF is 456, then what is the other number? Ans 1. 48 2. 120 3. 144 4. 72 Question ID : 26433063192 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 2", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 3, "q": "Find the median of the following data. 15, 30, 20, 10, 25, 35, 18, 21, 28 Ans 1. 30 2. 18 3. 25 4. 21 Question ID : 26433058695 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 4, "q": "Ans 1. 2 2. 0 3. 4 4. 1 Question ID : 264330126222 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 5, "q": "The annual growth rate of a city is 2%. If its population in the year 2020 was 1,50,000, then what will its population be in 2023? Ans 1. 1,59,181 2. 1,58,765 3. 1,58,413 4. 1,59,000 Question ID : 264330144221 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 6, "q": "In a 1200 m circular race, A and B start at the same time from the same position in the same direction at speeds of 18 km/h and 27 km/h, respectively. In how much time after the start of race will they meet for the first time on the track? Ans 1. 300 seconds 2. 480 seconds 3. 520 seconds 4. 240 seconds Question ID : 264330122718 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 2", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 7, "q": "The marked price of a television set is ₹18,000. A shopkeeper allows a discount of 40% and gets a profit of 10%. What is the cost price of the television set? Ans 1. 2. 3. 4. Question ID : 264330104510 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 8, "q": "The HCF of two numbers is 11 and their LCM is 693. If one of the numbers is 77, find the other. Ans 1. 66 2. 99 3. 55 4. 44 Question ID : 264330144225 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 2", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 9, "q": "Find the median of the following data. 129.75, 116.6, 12.3, 114.1, 136.6, 118.7, 13.5, 121.3 Ans 1. 116.60 2. 117.65 3. 118.75 4. 127.80 Question ID : 264330122995 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 2", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 10, "q": "The sum of the ages of Arun and Bharti is 24 years such that Arun is older. If the age of Arun and Bharti is doubled, the difference is 8 years. What is the age of Arun, in years? Ans 1. 28 2. 10 3. 16 4. 14 Question ID : 264330130056 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 11, "q": "Ans 1. 2. 3. 4. Question ID : 264330126220 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 2", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 12, "q": "The ages of father and son differ by 15 years. 5 years ago the father was 2 times old as his son. Find their present ages. Ans 1. 35 years, 20 years 2. 30 years, 15 years 3. 40 years, 25 years 4. 45 years, 30 years Question ID : 264330129979 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 13, "q": "The radii of two cylinders are in the ratio 2 : 1 and their heights are in the ratio 5 : 2. The ratio of their volumes is: Ans 1. 2. 3. 4. Question ID : 264330103642 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 3", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 14, "q": "Ans 1. 11/20 > 17/30 > 27/50 > 7/15 2. 17/30 > 11/20 > 27/50 > 7/15 3. 17/30 > 27/50 > 11/20 > 7/15 4. 7/15 > 11/20 > 27/50 >17/30 Question ID : 264330103969 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 15, "q": "In what ratio should rice costing Rs.67.5 per kg be mixed with rice costing Rs.60 per kg to get an average price of Rs.64 per kg? Ans 1. 8 : 7 2. 5 : 6 3. 6 : 5 4. 7 : 8 Question ID : 26433073081 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 16, "q": "If sums of the radii and distance between the centres of two circles are equal, then: Ans 1. the circles are concentric 2. the circles touch externally 3. the circles touch internally 4. the circles intersect each other Question ID : 264330122101 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 2", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 17, "q": "How many whole numbers lie between 112 and 122 ? Ans 1. 23 2. 24 3. 21 4. 22 Question ID : 264330123688 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 18, "q": "Gita purchases an apartment and pays EMI for that. Her monthly income is ₹80,000. She spends 15% on the education of her children, 40% on household affairs, sends 10% to GPF, saves 15% in a savings bank account and pays the rest of the amount as EMI. How much EMI does she pay? Ans 1. ₹14,000 2. ₹18,000 3. ₹16,000 4. ₹20,000 Question ID : 26433091535 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 3", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 19, "q": "A number is divisible by 3 only when: Ans 1. the difference of the sum of the odd and the even digits is divisible by 3 2. the sum of its digits is divisible by 3 3. the last digit is either 0 or an even number 4. the last two digits are divisible by 3 Question ID : 26433072988 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 2", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 20, "q": "The length of a rectangular plot is thrice its breadth. If the area of the rectangular plot is 2700 m2, then what is the breadth of the rectangular plot? Ans 1. 20 m 2. 12 m 3. 30 m 4. 28 m Question ID : 264330104211 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 3", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 21, "q": "A and B jointly start a business. The investment of A is equal to seven times the investment of B. Find the share of A (in ₹) in the annual profit of ₹2,75,000. Ans 1. 2,40,625 2. 2,45,625 3. 2,42,365 4. 2,41,225 Question ID : 264330121712 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 22, "q": "A can do a piece of work in 30 days, B in 50 days and C in 40 days. If A is assisted by B on one day and by C on the next day alternately, the work will be completed in: Ans 1. 2. 3. 4. Question ID : 26433082106 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 2", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 23, "q": "A sum of money doubles itself in 4 years at simple interest. In how much time will it become 7 times at the same rate of interest? Ans 1. 25 years 2. 23 years 3. 24 years 4. 21 years Question ID : 264330126196 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 3", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 24, "q": "Ten refrigerators and four mobile phones together cost ₹2,10,000 while six refrigerators and two mobile phones together cost ₹1,22,000. The cost (in ₹) of one refrigerator and two mobile phones is: Ans 1. 37000 2. 35200 3. 34500 4. 36000 Question ID : 264330126545 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 25, "q": "In an election between two candidates. 20% of the registered voters did not cast their vote and 40 votes were declared invalid. The winner got 42% of the registered votes and was declared the winner by 112 votes. The number of registered voters was: Ans 1. 1500 2. 1200 3. 1800 4. 3800 Question ID : 26433087350 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 3", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 26, "q": "The average of the square of first five even natural numbers is: Ans 1. 40 2. 44 3. 42 4. 46 Question ID : 264330104229 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 2", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 27, "q": "∆XYZ and ∆PQR are similar. XY : PQ = 6 : 1. Area of ∆PQR is 6 cm2. What is the area of ∆XYZ? Ans 1. 216 cm2 2. 6 cm2 3. 261 cm2 4. 36 cm2 Question ID : 264330122095 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 28, "q": "In grade 11 of a school, 40 students opted for Physics, 17 opted for Biology, and 20 opted for Chemistry. If the total number of students in grade 11 was 60, all of these students opted for at least one of the three subjects mentioned here, and exactly five of these students opted for all these three subjects, what is the probability that a randomly selected student of grade 11 of this school would have opted for exactly one of these three subjects? Ans 1. 0.75 2. 0.85 3. 0.90 4. 0.80 Question ID : 264330122861 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 29, "q": "AD is a tangent of a circle, and ABC is the secant. If AB = 8 cm and BC = 10 cm, then find the length of AD. Ans 1. 144 cm 2. 12.5 cm 3. 13.45 cm 4. 12 cm Question ID : 264330122097 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 30, "q": "A cube of side 5 cm, has been assembled using 125 cubes each of 1 cm edge. One cube is removed from the middle of each of the faces of the cube. What is the surface area (in cm2) of the remaining solid? Ans 1. 155 2. 144 3. 150 4. 174 Question ID : 26433063270 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : -- Section : Reasoning and General Intelligence", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 1, "q": "Select the number from among the given options that can replace the question mark (?) in the following series. 337, 354, 373, 394, 417, ? Ans 1. 446 2. 444 3. 440 4. 442 Question ID : 264330148531 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 1, "q": "Select the most appropriate option that can substitute the underlined segment in the given sentence. If there is no need to substitute it, select ‘No substitution required’. An ultralight airplane is very different from a conventional airplane. It is looking like a lawn chair with wings. Ans 1. No substitution required 2. look like 3. looked like 4. looks like Question ID : 26433063762 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 31, "q": "Identify whether the given statements are true or false. A. India’s working-age population was 900 million in 2021. B. In the next ten years, India’s working-age population will be more than 1 billion. Ans 1. A is false and B is true. 2. A is true and B is false. 3. Neither A nor B is true. 4. Both A and B are true. Question ID : 264330148474 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1 Comprehension: Read the given passage and answer the questions that follow. China and India together will account for more than a third of the estimated global population, which is expected to hit 8.045 billion by mid-year, according to the United Nations Population Fund’s (UNFPA) ‘State of World Population Report’ for 2023. But, contrary to public perception, population growth has been slowing in both countries – particularly in China, which recorded a population decline for the first time in six decades last year. China’s population fell in 2022 to 1.411 billion, down some 850,000 people from the previous year, according to China’s National Bureau of Statistics (NBS). The birth rate also fell to a record low of 6.77 births per 1,000 people, down from 7.52 a year earlier and the lowest level since the founding of Communist China in 1949. Along with the flagging population data, China also reported one of its worst economic growth numbers in nearly half a century last year, underscoring the steep challenges the country faces as its labor force shrinks and the ranks of the retired swell. India’s working-age population stands at more than 900 million, according to 2021 data from the Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development. This number is expected to hit more than 1 billion over the next decade, according to the Indian government. But these numbers could become a liability if policymakers do not create enough jobs, experts warned. SubQuestion No : 32", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 32, "q": "‘Along with the flagging population data.’ Here, ‘flagging’ means all of the following EXCEPT: Ans 1. ascending 2. waning 3. dwindling 4. contracting Question ID : 264330148475 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1 Comprehension: Read the given passage and answer the questions that follow. King Sagara, an ancestor of King Bhagiratha, once conducted an ashwamedha yagna to extend his dominion. When the horse went astray, the king sent his 60,000 sons to find the horse. Unfortunately, in the course of the quest, they ended up disrupting the intense meditation of sage Kapila, at whose abode they found the horse. Kapila burnt them all to ashes, sending them all to the netherworld—an act he instantly regretted when he realised what had happened. After breaking the news to King Sagara, he mentioned that the souls of King Sagara’s sons could attain salvation only if the heavenly Ganga could be persuaded to flow over their ashes. It was Bhagiratha, whose austere penance and devotion pleased Lord Shiva so much so that he persuaded Ganga to descend to the earth. Ganga consented, but the problem arose that the earth would probably be unable to bear the intensity of Ganga’s flow and even be shattered in the process. Thus, a solution was devised: Ganga would first land on Shiva’s head and the locks of his hair would minimise the impact. Still, the force of Ganga’s landing was such that it split into seven tributaries, three of which flowed east and three of them west. The seventh stream followed King Bhagiratha to the place where his ancestor’s ashes lay. The river’s waters instantly purified them. This is also the origin of the belief that the Ganga’s waters can purify mortal souls of all their sins. SubQuestion No : 33", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 33, "q": "Identify the option that arranges the given events in the correct sequence of their occurence. A. King Sagara’s sons were burnt by sage Kapila. B. King Bhagiratha persuaded Ganga to flow to the earth. C. King Sagara performed an ashwamedha yagna. D. The souls of the dead sons would not get salvation until Ganga flowed over their ashes. E. However, the flow had to be restrained by Shiva by holding it in his locks. Ans 1. CAEDB 2. CADBE 3. ACEBD 4. ADCBE Question ID : 264330148469 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 2 Comprehension: Read the given passage and answer the questions that follow. King Sagara, an ancestor of King Bhagiratha, once conducted an ashwamedha yagna to extend his dominion. When the horse went astray, the king sent his 60,000 sons to find the horse. Unfortunately, in the course of the quest, they ended up disrupting the intense meditation of sage Kapila, at whose abode they found the horse. Kapila burnt them all to ashes, sending them all to the netherworld—an act he instantly regretted when he realised what had happened. After breaking the news to King Sagara, he mentioned that the souls of King Sagara’s sons could attain salvation only if the heavenly Ganga could be persuaded to flow over their ashes. It was Bhagiratha, whose austere penance and devotion pleased Lord Shiva so much so that he persuaded Ganga to descend to the earth. Ganga consented, but the problem arose that the earth would probably be unable to bear the intensity of Ganga’s flow and even be shattered in the process. Thus, a solution was devised: Ganga would first land on Shiva’s head and the locks of his hair would minimise the impact. Still, the force of Ganga’s landing was such that it split into seven tributaries, three of which flowed east and three of them west. The seventh stream followed King Bhagiratha to the place where his ancestor’s ashes lay. The river’s waters instantly purified them. This is also the origin of the belief that the Ganga’s waters can purify mortal souls of all their sins. SubQuestion No : 34", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 34, "q": "This story is a: Ans 1. true story 2. historical story 3. fable 4. mythological story Question ID : 264330148468 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 2 Comprehension: Read the given passage and answer the questions that follow. King Sagara, an ancestor of King Bhagiratha, once conducted an ashwamedha yagna to extend his dominion. When the horse went astray, the king sent his 60,000 sons to find the horse. Unfortunately, in the course of the quest, they ended up disrupting the intense meditation of sage Kapila, at whose abode they found the horse. Kapila burnt them all to ashes, sending them all to the netherworld—an act he instantly regretted when he realised what had happened. After breaking the news to King Sagara, he mentioned that the souls of King Sagara’s sons could attain salvation only if the heavenly Ganga could be persuaded to flow over their ashes. It was Bhagiratha, whose austere penance and devotion pleased Lord Shiva so much so that he persuaded Ganga to descend to the earth. Ganga consented, but the problem arose that the earth would probably be unable to bear the intensity of Ganga’s flow and even be shattered in the process. Thus, a solution was devised: Ganga would first land on Shiva’s head and the locks of his hair would minimise the impact. Still, the force of Ganga’s landing was such that it split into seven tributaries, three of which flowed east and three of them west. The seventh stream followed King Bhagiratha to the place where his ancestor’s ashes lay. The river’s waters instantly purified them. This is also the origin of the belief that the Ganga’s waters can purify mortal souls of all their sins. SubQuestion No : 35", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 35, "q": "The above story is mainly about: Ans 1. Lord Shiva holding the Ganga in his locks 2. the ashwamedha yagna by King Sagara 3. the coming of the river Ganga to the earth 4. the sage Kapila’s anger for King Sagara’s sons Question ID : 264330148467 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 3 Comprehension: Read the given passage and answer the questions that follow. King Sagara, an ancestor of King Bhagiratha, once conducted an ashwamedha yagna to extend his dominion. When the horse went astray, the king sent his 60,000 sons to find the horse. Unfortunately, in the course of the quest, they ended up disrupting the intense meditation of sage Kapila, at whose abode they found the horse. Kapila burnt them all to ashes, sending them all to the netherworld—an act he instantly regretted when he realised what had happened. After breaking the news to King Sagara, he mentioned that the souls of King Sagara’s sons could attain salvation only if the heavenly Ganga could be persuaded to flow over their ashes. It was Bhagiratha, whose austere penance and devotion pleased Lord Shiva so much so that he persuaded Ganga to descend to the earth. Ganga consented, but the problem arose that the earth would probably be unable to bear the intensity of Ganga’s flow and even be shattered in the process. Thus, a solution was devised: Ganga would first land on Shiva’s head and the locks of his hair would minimise the impact. Still, the force of Ganga’s landing was such that it split into seven tributaries, three of which flowed east and three of them west. The seventh stream followed King Bhagiratha to the place where his ancestor’s ashes lay. The river’s waters instantly purified them. This is also the origin of the belief that the Ganga’s waters can purify mortal souls of all their sins. SubQuestion No : 36", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 36, "q": "‘It was Bhagiratha, whose austere penance….’ The word ‘austere’ here means: Ans 1. severe 2. rustic 3. bare 4. subdued Question ID : 264330148470 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4 Comprehension: In the following passage, some words have been deleted. Read the passage carefully and select the most appropriate option to fill in each blank. Astronomers have discovered 62 new moons orbiting the ringed planet Saturn. Though some of the moons had been (1)________ as early as 2019, it takes more than sighting an object close to a planet to (2) ________ it is a moon and not an asteroid making a brief close passage to that planet. Performing a painstaking (3) ________ of matching objects detected on different nights over the course of 24 months, the team tracked 63 objects that they ended up confirming as moons. One of (4) ________ satellites was revealed back in 2021, with the remaining 62 moons gradually announced over the past few weeks. SubQuestion No : 37", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 37, "q": "Select the most appropriate option to fill in blank no. 3. Ans 1. progress 2. practice 3. process 4. product Question ID : 264330148464 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 2 Comprehension: In the following passage, some words have been deleted. Read the passage carefully and select the most appropriate option to fill in each blank. Astronomers have discovered 62 new moons orbiting the ringed planet Saturn. Though some of the moons had been (1)________ as early as 2019, it takes more than sighting an object close to a planet to (2) ________ it is a moon and not an asteroid making a brief close passage to that planet. Performing a painstaking (3) ________ of matching objects detected on different nights over the course of 24 months, the team tracked 63 objects that they ended up confirming as moons. One of (4) ________ satellites was revealed back in 2021, with the remaining 62 moons gradually announced over the past few weeks. SubQuestion No : 38", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 38, "q": "Select the most appropriate option to fill in blank no. 1. Ans 1. spotted 2. spot 3. spotting 4. spots Question ID : 264330148462 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1 Comprehension: In the following passage, some words have been deleted. Read the passage carefully and select the most appropriate option to fill in each blank. Astronomers have discovered 62 new moons orbiting the ringed planet Saturn. Though some of the moons had been (1)________ as early as 2019, it takes more than sighting an object close to a planet to (2) ________ it is a moon and not an asteroid making a brief close passage to that planet. Performing a painstaking (3) ________ of matching objects detected on different nights over the course of 24 months, the team tracked 63 objects that they ended up confirming as moons. One of (4) ________ satellites was revealed back in 2021, with the remaining 62 moons gradually announced over the past few weeks. SubQuestion No : 39", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 39, "q": "Select the most appropriate option to fill in blank no. 4. Ans 1. that 2. those 3. this 4. these Question ID : 264330148465 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4 Comprehension: In the following passage, some words have been deleted. Read the passage carefully and select the most appropriate option to fill in each blank. Astronomers have discovered 62 new moons orbiting the ringed planet Saturn. Though some of the moons had been (1)________ as early as 2019, it takes more than sighting an object close to a planet to (2) ________ it is a moon and not an asteroid making a brief close passage to that planet. Performing a painstaking (3) ________ of matching objects detected on different nights over the course of 24 months, the team tracked 63 objects that they ended up confirming as moons. One of (4) ________ satellites was revealed back in 2021, with the remaining 62 moons gradually announced over the past few weeks. SubQuestion No : 40", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 40, "q": "Select the most appropriate option to fill in blank no. 2. Ans 1. sanction 2. confirm 3. consent 4. settle Question ID : 264330148463 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 2 Section : General Awareness", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 1, "q": "Which of the following statements about enzymes in the human body is/are correct? Statement A: Maltase is present in the saliva and breaks the sugar maltose into glucose. Statement B: Amylase is present in the saliva and helps change starches into sugars. Ans 1. Neither A nor B 2. Only A 3. Both A and B 4. Only B Question ID : 264330148625 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 1, "q": "Ans 1. 2. 3. 4. Question ID : 264330148380 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1", "o": [], "a": null}]});
