window.PYQ_OCR['ssc-chsl'].push({t:'ssc chsl 2024 05 jul shift 2',q:[{"n": 1, "q": "The following sentence has been split into four segments. Identify the segment that contains a grammatical error. We has travelled / to many states / of India to get / an essence of its diversity. Ans 1. an essence of its diversity 2. We has travelled 3. to many states 4. of India to get", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 2, "q": "Select the option that corrects the following sentence. All tickets of the FIFA World Cup have been sold away. Ans 1. All tickets of the FIFA World Cup have been sold among. 2. All tickets of the FIFA World Cup have been sold out. 3. All tickets of the FIFA World Cup have been sold into. 4. All tickets of the FIFA World Cup have been sold across.", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 3, "q": "Select the most appropriate option to fill in the blank. The captain dropped the trophy while he ________the victory with his teammates. Ans 1. celebrated 2. was celebrating 3. is celebrating 4. celebrates", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 4, "q": "The following sentence has been split into four segments. Identify the segment that contains a grammatical error. The soldiers / were selected / on the section / of ‘gallantry of spirits’. Ans 1. were selected 2. The soldiers 3. of ‘gallantry of spirits’. 4. on the section Comprehension: In the following passage, some words have been deleted. Read the passage carefully and select the most appropriate option to fill in each blank. For decades, humans have tried to theorise the origin and evolution of the universe. Many theories have been proposed and rejected. However, the Big Bang theory has been the most (1) ______ accepted. According to this theory, the universe began as a single point, or singularity, around 13.8 billion years ago. This singularity contained all the matter and energy that would eventually (2)______ the stars, galaxies and other structures that make up our universe today. The Big Bang theory is supported by a (3)______ of observational evidence, including the cosmic microwave background radiation, the (4)_______ of light elements in the universe and the large-scale structure of the cosmos. Despite its success, the Big Bang theory is still an active area of research, with scientists seeking to better understand the earliest moments of the universe and the (5)______ of dark matter and energy. SubQuestion No : 5", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 5, "q": "Select the most appropriate option to fill in blank number 1. Ans 1. vastly 2. largely 3. loosely 4. widely Comprehension: In the following passage, some words have been deleted. Read the passage carefully and select the most appropriate option to fill in each blank. For decades, humans have tried to theorise the origin and evolution of the universe. Many theories have been proposed and rejected. However, the Big Bang theory has been the most (1) ______ accepted. According to this theory, the universe began as a single point, or singularity, around 13.8 billion years ago. This singularity contained all the matter and energy that would eventually (2)______ the stars, galaxies and other structures that make up our universe today. The Big Bang theory is supported by a (3)______ of observational evidence, including the cosmic microwave background radiation, the (4)_______ of light elements in the universe and the large-scale structure of the cosmos. Despite its success, the Big Bang theory is still an active area of research, with scientists seeking to better understand the earliest moments of the universe and the (5)______ of dark matter and energy. SubQuestion No : 6", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 6, "q": "Select the most appropriate option to fill in blank number 2. Ans 1. destroy 2. form 3. design 4. prepare Comprehension: In the following passage, some words have been deleted. Read the passage carefully and select the most appropriate option to fill in each blank. For decades, humans have tried to theorise the origin and evolution of the universe. Many theories have been proposed and rejected. However, the Big Bang theory has been the most (1) ______ accepted. According to this theory, the universe began as a single point, or singularity, around 13.8 billion years ago. This singularity contained all the matter and energy that would eventually (2)______ the stars, galaxies and other structures that make up our universe today. The Big Bang theory is supported by a (3)______ of observational evidence, including the cosmic microwave background radiation, the (4)_______ of light elements in the universe and the large-scale structure of the cosmos. Despite its success, the Big Bang theory is still an active area of research, with scientists seeking to better understand the earliest moments of the universe and the (5)______ of dark matter and energy. SubQuestion No : 7", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 7, "q": "Select the most appropriate option to fill in blank number 3. Ans 1. rich 2. store 3. wealth 4. debt Comprehension: In the following passage, some words have been deleted. Read the passage carefully and select the most appropriate option to fill in each blank. For decades, humans have tried to theorise the origin and evolution of the universe. Many theories have been proposed and rejected. However, the Big Bang theory has been the most (1) ______ accepted. According to this theory, the universe began as a single point, or singularity, around 13.8 billion years ago. This singularity contained all the matter and energy that would eventually (2)______ the stars, galaxies and other structures that make up our universe today. The Big Bang theory is supported by a (3)______ of observational evidence, including the cosmic microwave background radiation, the (4)_______ of light elements in the universe and the large-scale structure of the cosmos. Despite its success, the Big Bang theory is still an active area of research, with scientists seeking to better understand the earliest moments of the universe and the (5)______ of dark matter and energy. SubQuestion No : 8", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 8, "q": "Select the most appropriate option to fill in blank number 4. Ans 1. plenty 2. fortune 3. abundance 4. success Comprehension: In the following passage, some words have been deleted. Read the passage carefully and select the most appropriate option to fill in each blank. For decades, humans have tried to theorise the origin and evolution of the universe. Many theories have been proposed and rejected. However, the Big Bang theory has been the most (1) ______ accepted. According to this theory, the universe began as a single point, or singularity, around 13.8 billion years ago. This singularity contained all the matter and energy that would eventually (2)______ the stars, galaxies and other structures that make up our universe today. The Big Bang theory is supported by a (3)______ of observational evidence, including the cosmic microwave background radiation, the (4)_______ of light elements in the universe and the large-scale structure of the cosmos. Despite its success, the Big Bang theory is still an active area of research, with scientists seeking to better understand the earliest moments of the universe and the (5)______ of dark matter and energy. SubQuestion No : 9", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 9, "q": "Select the most appropriate option to fill in blank number 5. Ans 1. brand 2. environment 3. nature 4. capture", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 10, "q": "Select the most appropriate meaning of the given idiom. Bag and baggage Ans 1. By force 2. With all goods 3. Fair and honest 4. At the service", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 11, "q": "Select the most appropriate option that can substitute the underlined segment in the given sentence. Employers in many developing countries report that a lack of skilled workers is a major and increasing bottleneck for their operations, affected their capacity to innovate. Ans 1. effect their capacity 2. affecting their capacity 3. effecting their capacity 4. affect their capacity", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 12, "q": "Select the most appropriate option that can substitute the underlined word in the given sentence. The dedicated teacher laboured assiduously to aid her pupils in achieving success. Ans 1. committed 2. un-biased 3. uninvolved 4. apathetic", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 13, "q": "Select the most appropriate option to fill in the blank. Which _________ do you usually take to reach your office? Ans 1. route 2. rude 3. rout 4. root", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 14, "q": "Identify the most appropriate ANTONYM of the underlined word in the given sentence. The vendor said that the apples were of superior quality. Ans 1. Small 2. Inferior 3. Excellent 4. Distasteful", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 15, "q": "Select the most appropriate meaning of the underlined idiom. The United Nations is working to eliminate the vicious cycle of poverty. Ans 1. Strength of something 2. Loophole of something 3. One problem causes other 4. The barrier of poverty", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 16, "q": "Select the most appropriate ANTONYM of the underlined word in the given sentence. Essays must be concise . Ans 1. Total 2. Precise 3. Lengthy 4. Excise", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 17, "q": "Read the sentence carefully and select the most appropriate option to substitute the underlined part. The clamour distracted the priest and made him angry. Ans 1. loud and confused noise 2. introduction of new things 3. humorous deception 4. narrow-mindedness", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 18, "q": "Select the most appropriate option that can substitute the underlined word segment in the following sentence. The girl which is wearing a blue shirt is my sister. Ans 1. who is wearing a blue shirt 2. which wear a blue shirt 3. who wear a blue shirt 4. which is wearing the blue shirt", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 19, "q": "The following sentence has been split into four segments. Identify the segment that contains a spelling error. The make-up room was filled / with incadescent lights / which added to the misery / of those subjected to make-up. Ans 1. of those subjected to make-up 2. The make-up room was filled 3. with incadescent lights 4. which added to the misery", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 20, "q": "Select the most appropriate ANTONYM of the underlined word. No one trusts her as her reasons are always explicit . Ans 1. Ambiguous 2. Exact 3. Precise 4. Distant", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 21, "q": "Select the correct collocation to complete the following sentence. He made __________ use of the opportunity to travel. Ans 1. entire 2. full 3. whole 4. total", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 22, "q": "Select the most appropriate synonym of the given word. Tedious Ans 1. Working 2. Boring 3. Exciting 4. Happening", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 23, "q": "Select the most appropriate homophone to fill in the blank. Arun knows perfectly well how to mix the food items with __________. Ans 1. source 2. saws 3. sauce 4. sause", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 24, "q": "Select the most appropriate synonym of the given word. Permit Ans 1. Flout 2. Abandon 3. Approve 4. Disgrace", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 25, "q": "Select the INCORRECTLY spelt word. Ans 1. Immaculate 2. Immense 3. Irreverent 4. Innoculate Section : General Intelligence", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 1, "q": "RTVX is related to SUWY in a certain way based on the English alphabetical order. In the same way, KMOQ is related to LNPR. To which of the following is FHJL related, following the same logic? Ans 1. GHJK 2. GIJK 3. GIKN 4. GIKM", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 1, "q": "Ans 1. 3 2. 4 3. 2 4. 5", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 1, "q": "In 2026, which country will host Asian Games? Ans 1. Nepal 2. China 3. India 4. Japan", "o": [], "a": null}]});
window.PYQ_OCR['ssc-chsl'].push({t:'ssc chsl tier 1 shift 2',q:[{"n": 1, "q": "Fill in the blank with an appropriate option. The social ______ is going to meet with all of us tomorrow with the plans so we can make a decision. Ans 1. army 2. worker 3. labour 4. toddler Question ID : 264330124677 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 2", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 2, "q": "Choose the word that is opposite in meaning to the given word. Inept Ans 1. Wanting 2. Barred 3. Competent 4. Callow Question ID : 264330124277 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 3", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 3, "q": "Find the part of the given sentence that has an error in it. If there is no error, choose ‘No error’. I just don’t like the themes of todays music. Ans 1. No error 2. I just don’t 3. like the themes of 4. todays music. Question ID : 264330124603 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 2", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 4, "q": "Choose the word that means the same as the given word. Instigate Ans 1. Deterrence 2. Settle 3. Complaisance 4. Raise Question ID : 264330124623 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 3", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 5, "q": "Some parts of one or more sentences have been jumbled up, and labelled A, B, C and D. Select the option that gives the correct sequence in which these parts can be rearranged to form a meaningful and grammatically correct sentence. At Paris, just after dark A. of meditation and a meerschaum, in company B. one gusty evening in the autumn C. of 18, I was enjoying the twofold luxury D. with my friend Auguste Dupin, in his little back library Ans 1. ADBC 2. CDBA 3. BCAD 4. DCBA Question ID : 264330125743 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 2", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 6, "q": "Select the word that is closest in meaning (SYNONYM) to the word given below. WHIMSICAL Ans 1. RESPECTFUL 2. HUMILIATED 3. WEAK 4. FUNNY Question ID : 264330125782 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 7, "q": "The given sentence is in active voice. Change the voice of the sentence. Select the correct option from the sentences given in options. The story explores the conflicting range of human emotions. Ans 1. The conflicting range of human emotions had explored by the story. 2. The conflicting range of human emotions is explored by the story. 3. The conflicting range of human emotions did explored by the story. 4. The conflicting range of human emotions has explored by the story. Question ID : 264330125837 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 2", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 8, "q": "Choose the word that can substitute the given group of words. A lover of oneself, of one’s advancement Ans 1. Egoist 2. Philistine 3. Mercenary 4. Cynic Question ID : 264330124335 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 9, "q": "In the following question, out of the given four alternatives, select the alternative which best expresses the meaning of the Idiom/Phrase. Over and above Ans 1. In addition to 2. Highest rank 3. To sum up the conversation 4. Above all Question ID : 264330124617 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 10, "q": "Choose the word that can substitute the given group of words. Book giving information about everything Ans 1. Phonebook 2. Encyclopedia 3. Thesis 4. Dictionary Question ID : 264330124231 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 2", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 11, "q": "Choose the sentence with no spelling error. Ans 1. The joy definitely lies in cooking for others. 2. The joy definitely lyes in cooking for others. 3. The joy definitely lies in cokking for others. 4. The joy defintely lies in cooking for others. Question ID : 264330124620 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 12, "q": "Fill in the blank with an appropriate option. In this engineering design project you will learn how to build an infinity mirror, with built-in lights that make the mirror look like a deep ______ with no end. Ans 1. tunnel 2. signal 3. funeral 4. lodge Question ID : 264330124210 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 13, "q": "Parts of the following sentence are given as options. Identify the part that contains a grammatical error. If there is no error, select 'No error'. He has been / told many a times to / mind his manners. Ans 1. mind his manners. 2. No error 3. told many a times to 4. He has been Question ID : 264330125840 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 14, "q": "Fill in the blank with an appropriate option. In humans, lack of sleep leads to ______ memory and reduced cognitive abilities. Ans 1. impaired 2. witnessed 3. attended 4. thankless Question ID : 264330124444 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 15, "q": "Choose the incorrectly spelt word. Ans 1. Practical 2. Released 3. Glowing 4. Frighter Question ID : 264330124619 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 16, "q": "Rearrange the parts of the sentence in correct order. P. more stringent mobility control and physical distancing policies Q. East Asian governments (except for Japan) implemented R. as well as more comprehensive testing, tracing S. and isolation policies since the early stages Ans 1. PSRQ 2. QPRS 3. QSPR 4. PRSQ Question ID : 264330124612 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 2", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 17, "q": "Select the correct indirect form of the given sentence. Gloria said, “His relatives are landing tomorrow.” Ans 1. Gloria said that his relatives are landing the next day. 2. Gloria said that his relatives were landing the next day. 3. Gloria said that his relatives have been landing the next day. 4. Gloria said that his relatives were landing the previous day. Question ID : 264330124602 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 2", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 18, "q": "Choose the word that means the same as the given word. Calibrate Ans 1. Gauze 2. Assail 3. Gauge 4. Affront Question ID : 264330124312 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 3", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 19, "q": "Select the most appropriate meaning of the given idiom. Ace in the hole Ans 1. To create noisy disturbances so that competitors are unable to work. 2. A major advantage that one keeps hidden until an ideal time. 3. To attempt to do the impossible. 4. To suffer an injury on the lower body. Question ID : 264330125854 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 2", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 20, "q": "Select the most appropriate one-word substitution for the given group of words. A man who is womanish in his habits Ans 1. Infidel 2. Hooch 3. Effeminate 4. Indictment Question ID : 264330125805 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 3 Comprehension: In the following passage some of the words have been deleted. Read the passage carefully and select the correct answer for the given blank out of the four alternatives. People may seek fashion as part of (1) ______ they are and may want to be a fashion lover, which may lead them to spend more time (2) ______ out the latest fashion trends and more money than others on fashion products. We all know the good feeling that goes (3) ______ walking out of a store with a new shade of lipstick or after ordering a killer pair of boots online. They call it retail therapy for a reason, and more than one scientific study has (4) ______ its effectiveness. Shopping takes time and concentration, whether it is being done online (5) ______ in your favourite store. SubQuestion No : 21", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 21, "q": "Select the most appropriate option to fill in blank number 1. Ans 1. whom 2. which 3. who 4. whose Question ID : 264330124606 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 2 Comprehension: In the following passage some of the words have been deleted. Read the passage carefully and select the correct answer for the given blank out of the four alternatives. People may seek fashion as part of (1) ______ they are and may want to be a fashion lover, which may lead them to spend more time (2) ______ out the latest fashion trends and more money than others on fashion products. We all know the good feeling that goes (3) ______ walking out of a store with a new shade of lipstick or after ordering a killer pair of boots online. They call it retail therapy for a reason, and more than one scientific study has (4) ______ its effectiveness. Shopping takes time and concentration, whether it is being done online (5) ______ in your favourite store. SubQuestion No : 22", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 22, "q": "Select the most appropriate option to fill in blank number 2. Ans 1. seeking 2. making 3. freaking 4. doing Question ID : 264330124607 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1 Comprehension: In the following passage some of the words have been deleted. Read the passage carefully and select the correct answer for the given blank out of the four alternatives. People may seek fashion as part of (1) ______ they are and may want to be a fashion lover, which may lead them to spend more time (2) ______ out the latest fashion trends and more money than others on fashion products. We all know the good feeling that goes (3) ______ walking out of a store with a new shade of lipstick or after ordering a killer pair of boots online. They call it retail therapy for a reason, and more than one scientific study has (4) ______ its effectiveness. Shopping takes time and concentration, whether it is being done online (5) ______ in your favourite store. SubQuestion No : 23", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 23, "q": "Select the most appropriate option to fill in blank number 3. Ans 1. within 2. off in 3. up in 4. along with Question ID : 264330124608 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4 Comprehension: In the following passage some of the words have been deleted. Read the passage carefully and select the correct answer for the given blank out of the four alternatives. People may seek fashion as part of (1) ______ they are and may want to be a fashion lover, which may lead them to spend more time (2) ______ out the latest fashion trends and more money than others on fashion products. We all know the good feeling that goes (3) ______ walking out of a store with a new shade of lipstick or after ordering a killer pair of boots online. They call it retail therapy for a reason, and more than one scientific study has (4) ______ its effectiveness. Shopping takes time and concentration, whether it is being done online (5) ______ in your favourite store. SubQuestion No : 24", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 24, "q": "Select the most appropriate option to fill in blank number 4. Ans 1. backed up 2. summed up 3. held back 4. sold on Question ID : 264330124609 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 2 Comprehension: In the following passage some of the words have been deleted. Read the passage carefully and select the correct answer for the given blank out of the four alternatives. People may seek fashion as part of (1) ______ they are and may want to be a fashion lover, which may lead them to spend more time (2) ______ out the latest fashion trends and more money than others on fashion products. We all know the good feeling that goes (3) ______ walking out of a store with a new shade of lipstick or after ordering a killer pair of boots online. They call it retail therapy for a reason, and more than one scientific study has (4) ______ its effectiveness. Shopping takes time and concentration, whether it is being done online (5) ______ in your favourite store. SubQuestion No : 25", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 25, "q": "Select the most appropriate option to fill in blank number 5. Ans 1. or 2. and 3. so 4. if Question ID : 264330124610 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1 Section : General Intelligence", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 1, "q": "Ans 1. 2. 3. 4. Question ID : 264330126963 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 2", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 1, "q": "Ans 1. 2. 3. 4. Question ID : 264330127945 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 3", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 1, "q": "Which article of the Indian constitution is related with the Separation of judiciary from executive? Ans 1. 50 2. 41 3. 51 4. 40 Question ID : 264330125053 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 3", "o": [], "a": null}]});

